    {
      "id": "MR-C159-gelo",
      "sequence": 7611,
      "title": "मी गेलो (mī gelo) — the past, one small ending at a time",
      "headword": "मी गेलो",
      "romanization": "mī gelo",
      "gloss": "I went — the plain past agrees with the person or thing that did it",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:327eb555f324be5e",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say घडणे (ghaḍṇe), \"to happen\", then मी, \"I\", and जाणे, \"to go\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: who did it?",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "काल मी पुण्याला गेलो. kāl mī puṇyālā gelo. — \"Yesterday I went to Pune.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The past shows who did it. A man says मी गेलो (mī gelo); a woman says मी गेले. With तो / ती, use तो गेला / ती गेली. With respect or several people, use तुम्ही गेलात. Hear the same gender endings you already know from माझा / माझी / माझं, now after -ल-."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: a few useful stems",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Most verbs put -ल- onto the stem: बसणे becomes बसलो, झोपणे becomes झोपलो, पडणे becomes पडला. Two everyday verbs change more: येणे becomes आलो / आली and होणे becomes झाला / झाली. Put नाही after the completed form for \"did not\": मी गेलो (mī gelo) नाही."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "\"Yesterday I went to Pune\" — kāl mī puṇyālā gelo or gele",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: \"Yesterday I went to Pune\" — *kāl mī puṇyālā gelo* or *gele*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "\"She came home in the evening\" — tī sandhyākāḷī gharī ālī",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: \"She came home in the evening\" — *tī sandhyākāḷī gharī ālī*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "\"We sat. We slept.\" — āmhī baslo. āmhī jhoplo.",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: \"We sat. We slept.\" — *āmhī baslo. āmhī jhoplo.*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "spoken": true,
              "id": "MR-C159-gelo-r1",
              "prompt": "Say that you went to Pune yesterday, then that she came home.",
              "assesses": [
