              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "त्याने काम केलं. tyāne kām kelaṁ. — \"He did the work.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With a past action done to something, the third-person doer takes -ने: तो becomes त्याने, ती becomes तिने, मीरा becomes मीराने. The first and second person stay मी and तू in ordinary Marathi: मी काम केलं."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: the verb follows the object",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The ending now follows what was acted on: त्याने आंबा खाल्ला, because आंबा is masculine; मी पोळी खाल्ली, because पोळी is feminine; त्याने पुस्तक वाचलं, because पुस्तक is neuter. So त्याने कुत्रा पाहिला has पाहिला following masculine कुत्रा."
            }
          ]
        },
